{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "https://github.com/frankp/process-runtime/schemas/model-manifest.schema.json",
  "title": "ModelManifest",
  "description": "Blueprint v3.1 §4.1: ports, mathematics, derivatives, initialization, validity, implementation artifact, execution requirements. §5.2 requires derivatives to be declared per output and operating regime, with `unavailable` an honest answer; §5.1 fixes the three execution classes. The `status` field separates a manifest that declares intended behavior from one describing implemented code: in P01 nothing is implemented, so every SYN-001 manifest is `declared` with `derivatives.method: unavailable`. ADR 0008 D3 added the required per-equation `accumulation` declaration.",
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "required": [
    "id",
    "version",
    "status",
    "ports",
    "mathematics",
    "derivatives",
    "initialization",
    "validity",
    "implementation_artifact",
    "execution_requirements"
  ],
  "properties": {
    "id": { "type": "string", "pattern": "^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9_.:-]*$" },
    "version": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 },
    "status": {
      "enum": ["declared", "implemented", "tested", "reviewed", "released"],
      "description": "`declared` means this manifest states intended behavior and no implementation exists yet. It is never evidence that the model works."
    },
    "title": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 },
    "description": { "type": "string" },
    "introduced_by_package": {
      "type": "string",
      "pattern": "^[PKTMSR][0-9]{2}$",
      "description": "The work package that will implement the model, so a declared manifest names its owner."
    },
    "ports": {
      "type": "array",
      "minItems": 1,
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "required": [
          "name",
          "kind",
          "direction",
          "multiplicity",
          "component_mapping",
          "state_definition",
          "phase_capabilities"
        ],
        "properties": {
          "name": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 },
          "kind": { "enum": ["material", "energy", "signal"] },
          "direction": { "enum": ["inlet", "outlet"] },
          "multiplicity": {
            "oneOf": [
              { "type": "integer", "minimum": 1 },
              { "const": "many" }
            ],
            "description": "How many connections the port accepts; 'many' for a mixer inlet."
          },
          "component_mapping": {
            "oneOf": [
              { "const": "revision_component_set" },
              { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 } },
              { "type": "null" }
            ],
            "description": "How the port's component indices map to the revision's component set; null for a non-material port."
          },
          "state_definition": {
            "oneOf": [{ "const": "nTP-v1" }, { "type": "null" }],
            "description": "ADR 0001 D2.1. `nTP-v1` is component molar flows in mol/s, absolute T in K and P in Pa. An alternative definition enters only through an adapter that declares its own ID. Null for a non-material port."
          },
          "phase_capabilities": {
            "type": "array",
            "uniqueItems": true,
            "items": { "enum": ["liquid", "vapor", "vapor_liquid"] },
            "description": "Declared capability, not a result. The phase *signature* of a stream is produced by evaluation (ADR 0001 D2.4)."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mathematics": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "oneOf": [
        { "required": ["equations"] },
        { "required": ["evaluator_reference"] }
      ],
      "properties": {
        "equations": {
          "type": "array",
          "minItems": 0,
          "description": "An empty list is a positive assertion that the model contributes no equation to the system — the honest description of a boundary sink. It is not a placeholder for equations still to be written.",
          "items": {
            "type": "object",
            "additionalProperties": false,
            "required": ["id", "statement", "dependencies", "conditional_class", "accumulation"],
            "properties": {
              "id": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 },
              "statement": {
                "type": "string",
                "minLength": 1,
                "description": "Human-readable residual statement. The serialized expression vocabulary arrives with K01; P01 does not invent one."
              },
              "dependencies": {
                "type": "array",
                "items": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 }
              },
              "dimension": {
                "$ref": "https://github.com/frankp/process-runtime/schemas/quantity.schema.json#/$defs/dimension"
              },
              "conditional_class": {
                "enum": ["unconditional", "phase_conditional", "regime_conditional"],
                "description": "Blueprint §4.1 'conditional class': whether the equation is always present or belongs to an active set."
              },
              "source": { "type": "string" },
              "accumulation": { "$ref": "#/$defs/accumulation" }
            },
            "if": {
              "properties": {
                "accumulation": {
                  "properties": { "kind": { "enum": ["holdup_balance", "zero_holdup_balance"] } }
                }
              }
            },
            "then": { "required": ["dimension"] }
          }
        },
        "evaluator_reference": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 }
      }
    },
    "derivatives": {
      "type": "array",
      "minItems": 1,
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "required": ["output", "with_respect_to", "method"],
        "properties": {
          "output": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 },
          "with_respect_to": {
            "type": "array",
            "minItems": 1,
            "items": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 }
          },
          "method": {
            "enum": [
              "analytic",
              "ad",
              "implicit",
              "finite_difference",
              "unavailable"
            ],
            "description": "Blueprint §5.2, declared per output. `unavailable` is reported as absent and is never replaced with fabricated zeros."
          },
          "regime": { "type": "string" },
          "notes": { "type": "string" }
        }
      }
    },
    "initialization": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "required": ["strategy", "notes"],
      "properties": {
        "strategy": {
          "enum": ["none", "registered_initializer", "local_initializer", "upstream_propagation"]
        },
        "registered_initializer": { "type": ["string", "null"] },
        "notes": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 }
      },
      "description": "An initializer supplies a guess. A guess is not a specification and a poor guess is not proof of infeasibility (blueprint §4.3)."
    },
    "validity": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "required": ["domain", "limitations"],
      "properties": {
        "domain": {
          "type": "object",
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "properties": {
            "temperature_K": { "$ref": "#/$defs/interval" },
            "pressure_Pa": { "$ref": "#/$defs/interval" },
            "components": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 }
            },
            "phases": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": { "enum": ["liquid", "vapor", "vapor_liquid", "zero_flow"] }
            }
          }
        },
        "limitations": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 },
          "description": "Known limits of the declared model. An empty list asserts there are none, so it is used only when that is true."
        }
      }
    },
    "implementation_artifact": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "required": ["state", "module", "artifact_hash"],
      "properties": {
        "state": {
          "enum": ["not_implemented", "source", "compiled_artifact"],
          "description": "`not_implemented` with a null module is the honest P01 answer; it must not be dressed up as a source reference."
        },
        "module": { "type": ["string", "null"] },
        "artifact_hash": { "type": ["string", "null"], "pattern": "^[0-9a-f]{64}$" },
        "planned_package": { "type": "string", "pattern": "^[PKTMSR][0-9]{2}$" }
      }
    },
    "execution_requirements": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "required": ["execution_class", "thread_safety", "evaluation_cost_class"],
      "properties": {
        "execution_class": {
          "enum": ["native_equation", "explicit_reduced", "experiment_provider"],
          "description": "Blueprint §5.1."
        },
        "thread_safety": { "enum": ["unknown", "not_thread_safe", "thread_safe"] },
        "evaluation_cost_class": { "enum": ["unknown", "cheap", "moderate", "expensive"] },
        "property_provider": { "type": ["string", "null"] },
        "reference_convention": {
          "type": ["string", "null"],
          "description": "Enthalpy flows are comparable only within one provider implementation hash, data hash and reference convention (ADR 0001 D5.2)."
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "$defs": {
    "accumulation": {
      "description": "ADR 0008 D3. Every equation says what it conserves. `algebraic`: not a conservation row; a zero row of any mass matrix. `zero_holdup_balance`: a conservation balance whose holdup is identically zero by the model's definition (junction, divider) — a zero row of M by physics, with the reason stated. `holdup_balance`: a conservation balance whose steady-state form is the zero-accumulation limit of d(holdup)/dt = F_row; names the accumulated quantity and its dimension. Balance rows are written F_row = inflow − outflow + sources (D3.3). No default: a forgotten declaration is invalid, never `algebraic`.",
      "oneOf": [
        {
          "type": "object",
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "required": ["kind"],
          "properties": { "kind": { "const": "algebraic" } }
        },
        {
          "type": "object",
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "required": ["kind", "reason"],
          "properties": {
            "kind": { "const": "zero_holdup_balance" },
            "reason": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 }
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "object",
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "required": ["kind", "holdup"],
          "properties": {
            "kind": { "const": "holdup_balance" },
            "holdup": {
              "type": "object",
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "required": ["symbol", "quantity", "dimension"],
              "properties": {
                "symbol": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 },
                "quantity": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 },
                "dimension": {
                  "$ref": "https://github.com/frankp/process-runtime/schemas/quantity.schema.json#/$defs/dimension"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "interval": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "required": ["min", "max"],
      "properties": {
        "min": { "type": "number" },
        "max": { "type": "number" }
      }
    }
  }
}
